## Alternative considered: a seal test at every cold take

Instead of trusting the name fact, a cold take reads the seal bit of the node it has and takes a sealed one out of line (`ctr_own` = `term_rfc(t) ? ctr_seal(e, t, n) : term_loc(t)`, with the cold path behind `OUTLINE`). This closes the hole regardless of what the facts see and is smaller (+191 ttok), but the bit test lands on every cold take in every hot loop: tree-bitonic +2.2%, tree-matmul +0.3%, the rest flat. Routing every owned take through `ctr_take` (-78 ttok) costs tree-bitonic +14%, and inlining the cold path +35%, from `heap_alloc` and `span_fade` inlined into the hot loops. The dispatch already ignores the seal bit and a two-arm if/else has no free slot for a third case, so there is no zero-cost dynamic placement.

