Bend is intended to prevent incorrect AI-generated code from passing through formal laws. If a proof file can omit laws or prove unrelated theorem names while still passing, an AI agent can generate a plausible-looking but incomplete proof file and receive a false success result.

The law/proof gate should enforce exact theorem coverage and validate that all imported laws are actually checked.

