Fixes #1146

`IO.random_u32` declares `IO(Result<&1, &1, U32 & String, U32>)`, and the C lane honours that: `io_sys_end` stores the `getrandom` errno and `io_res` turns a non-zero code into `io_fail(e, code, NULL)`. The JS lane called `crypto.getRandomValues` with no `try`, so a host whose WebCrypto throws ended the effect and the run, and a host with no `crypto` at all raised a `ReferenceError` on the name. The same program recovers on C and dies on JS.

```js
function io_random_u32() {
  try {
    return io_done(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0]);
  } catch (e) {
    return io_fail(typeof e?.errno === "number" ? Math.abs(e.errno) : 5);
  }
}
```

`io_fail(code)` is the JS lane's `Fail` and already prints `strerror(code)`, so the error carries the same `(code, message)` pair the C lane builds. WebCrypto gives no errno to forward, so EIO stands in — that is the same fallback `process_run.js` already uses when Bun throws without one. The `e?.` also covers a host that throws a non-object, which would otherwise throw again inside the catch.

## Test

`tests/io/random_u32_js_fail.bend` is the report's repro as a test: a host effect whose `.js` twin replaces `getRandomValues` with one that throws, then `IO.random_u32` read through the declared `Result`, printing the code rather than the message so the expectation does not depend on the platform's `strerror` text.

Without the fix the JS run prints `Error: entropy source failed` and exits 1, which is the reported symptom verbatim. With it, the program prints `fail 5`.

The `.bend` gets a `.js` twin only, so `gates/test.ts` drops the C lane — it never failed, and a C twin would have to fake a `getrandom` errno to test anything. That leaves this pinned to the lane that had the bug.

## Verification

Interpreted, JS-compiled and C-compiled runs, on `bun 1.4.2` / `clang`, at `dfeb0c59`:

| test | interp | js | c |
|---|---|---|---|
| `random_u32_js_fail` (new) | `fail 5` | `fail 5` | lane dropped |
| `random_u32` (existing) | `True` | `True` | `True` |

I also ran the whole `tests/io` directory through the interpreter before and after: 100/133 before, 101/134 after, with the 31 failures identical in both runs — they are the tests that expect a non-zero exit or a particular stream, which my local runner does not model the way `gates/test.ts` does. The new test is the only difference.

One thing I could not run here: the gate itself (`gates/test.ts`) shards tests across the mini cluster, so the C-lane build of the full suite is unverified locally, though `random_u32.c` is untouched and the C build of the existing test still compiles and passes.

`gates/repo.ts` allows both paths (`/^bend2\/effs\/[a-z0-9_]+\.(c|js)$/` and `/^tests\/[a-z]+\/[a-z0-9_]+\.(c|js)$/`), and the diff adds no tokens to `bend2/bend.ts` or `comp.ts`.

