Generate each backend with `bun bend2/main.ts probe.bend -o probe.c` / `-o probe.js`; compile C with `clang -std=c11 -O2 probe.c -lpthread -lm -o probe` and run `./probe --threads 1 --gpu off` / `bun probe.js`. The intended observable result is `error:9`, exit 0; the baseline aborts instead.

## Cause and review boundary

Both readiness loops only recover from `EINTR`. `select` reports `EBADF` for the whole set, so the receive handler is bypassed. A narrow fix can query descriptor flags only on that error path, resume the invalid descriptors' handlers, preserve valid waiters and deadlines, and leave other selector errors fatal.

