This handles the constructor-equality case without needing an `inj` helper. Model search can use an available equation directly, or build a total field projection and use ordinary rewrite/reflexivity. Fields must have non-dependent types; the kernel is unchanged.

This is not a general model-search fix: `k` and `pick` from the thread are not addressed. Erased evidence, unrelated fields and impossible result models stay out of scope. No root-constant backtracking.

