## What you did

Read `ring_push` and the host drain loop in `pool_rows` (`bend2/comp.ts`, main at d60b4c68) while reviewing #2079. I found this by reading the code. I haven't reproduced it.

## What happened

When `ring_push` finds the ring full, it has already reserved slot `pos` (comp.ts:4212). It posts `ERR_RING` and returns without writing the slot:

```c
u32 pos = a32_add(ring_put(H, r), 1);
if (pos - a32_load(ring_get(H, r)) >= RING_LEN) {
  err_post(H, ERR_RING);
  return;            // put is already past pos; slot pos keeps last lap's bit
}
```

The host drain loop (comp.ts:4760) snapshots `put` and spins until `get` reaches it. It never checks `err_seen`:

```c
u32 put0 = a32_load(ring_put(e.mem, rg));
while (*ring_get(e.mem, rg) != put0) {
  monk_step(e, stk, rg, put0, rg, 0, NULL);
}
```

In a drain turn, `task_deal` with stride 0 sends tasks to any ring through `H_CURSOR`, so another thread can push to `rg` while its owner drains it. If that push finds `rg` full, `put` has moved past `pos` but slot `pos` is never written. If the owner's `put0` snapshot is past `pos`, `monk_step` returns 0 on every call from then on (`(hi >> 31) != ring_lap(*get)`), and the loop never ends. The thread never reaches `n += 1` or signals `pool_join`, so the run hangs instead of failing with `ERR_RING`.

The device pass-1 loop (comp.ts:4577) checks `err_seen` and stops, so this only affects the host.

## What should happen

The run should stop and report `ERR_RING`. Two possible fixes:

- check `err_seen(e.mem)` in the drain loop, as the device loop does, or
- have `ring_push` write a slot the popper can skip (or undo the reservation) when the ring is full.

