### What you did

Linted a file with a long comment and one rule that returned one safe fix containing 16,000 adjacent one-character replacements. No `--fix` was used; the cost is in checking the rule's output, before applying anything. The rule builds the edits like this:

```js
const edits = Array.from({ length: 16000 }, (_, i) => ({
  span: { file: cx.root, beg: i + 1, end: i + 2 },
  text: "y",
}));
return [cx.diag({ message: "change comment", fixes: [{
  title: "change comment", applicability: "safe", edits,
}] })];
```

### What happened

`lint(file, [rule])` took 1,255, 1,232 and 1,228 ms after a warm `lint(file, [])`. The edit ranges are valid and disjoint, but validating one fix compares every edit against every other edit. #2258 is a different pass: picking edits across fixes for `--fix` after validation.

